{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02428",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 4.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.26,
      "end_seconds": 11.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.51,
      "end_seconds": 29.85,
      "duration_seconds": 17.34,
      "text": "Mainly cramping in my calves when I walk. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I took the morning off to come in today. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.11,
      "end_seconds": 38.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.43,
      "end_seconds": 49.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.95,
      "end_seconds": 51.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.99,
      "end_seconds": 56.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.38,
      "end_seconds": 60.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.62,
      "end_seconds": 79.15,
      "duration_seconds": 16.53,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get hair loss on my shins as well. The hair loss on my shins? That's been for two weeks. I've also had a slow-healing toe sore, for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.48,
      "end_seconds": 83.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.98,
      "end_seconds": 86.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.41,
      "end_seconds": 108.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Okay, a few quick ones: fever or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.85,
      "end_seconds": 112.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.25,
      "end_seconds": 117.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "A few quick ones: back pain or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.92,
      "end_seconds": 120.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.03,
      "end_seconds": 123.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.15,
      "end_seconds": 125.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.4,
      "end_seconds": 138.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.78,
      "end_seconds": 144.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.53,
      "end_seconds": 153.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.47,
      "end_seconds": 158.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Oh, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.67,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.89,
      "end_seconds": 174.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Atorvastatin, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.02,
      "end_seconds": 179.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.83,
      "end_seconds": 190.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "20 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. I had glimepiride at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.06,
      "end_seconds": 197.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.79,
      "end_seconds": 205.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes. I have high cholesterol, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.03,
      "end_seconds": 209.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay, a few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.57,
      "end_seconds": 233.33,
      "duration_seconds": 18.76,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I share a house with my brother. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.43,
      "end_seconds": 238.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.65,
      "end_seconds": 252.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.52,
      "end_seconds": 281.81,
      "duration_seconds": 18.29,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, respiratory rate 17, pulse is 81 beats a minute, weight 71 kilos, BP is 112 over 73, BMI works out to 21.4, temp 36.6 degrees, height 182 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.2,
      "end_seconds": 288.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.94,
      "end_seconds": 291.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.77,
      "end_seconds": 294.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.61,
      "end_seconds": 309.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "The pulses at the left foot are absent and the foot is cool and shiny."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.45,
      "end_seconds": 330.26,
      "duration_seconds": 15.81,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. So where does that leave us? It fits best with peripheral arterial disease. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. We shouldn't forget a nerve problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.61,
      "end_seconds": 336.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Hmm, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.27,
      "end_seconds": 358.14,
      "duration_seconds": 20.87,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like peripheral arterial disease, but I'd like to confirm. A cholesterol test is what I'd like next, for arterial disease. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 358.92,
      "end_seconds": 362.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I can book that for Wednesday at 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.66,
      "end_seconds": 367.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an ankle-brachial index because of claudication."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.84,
      "end_seconds": 371.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.95,
      "end_seconds": 385.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "An ultrasound of the leg arteries is what I'd like next, for claudication. I'd like you to take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day, long term. That's for arterial disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.74,
      "end_seconds": 389.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "How soon will it work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.44,
      "end_seconds": 405.03,
      "duration_seconds": 14.59,
      "text": "A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Let's plan a check in four weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.05,
      "end_seconds": 409.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.42,
      "end_seconds": 411.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}